separately before they can appear in Cost Explorer or on a cost allocation =
report</strong></p>

<p>A Cost Allocation Tag is a label that you or AWS assigns to an AWS resou=
rce. Each tag consists of a key and a value. For each resource, each tag ke=
y must be unique, and each tag key can have only one value. You can use tag=
s to organize your resources, and cost allocation tags to track your AWS co=
sts on a detailed level.</p>

<p>AWS provides two types of cost allocation tags, an AWS generated tags an=
d user-defined tags. AWS defines, creates, and applies the AWS generated ta=
gs for you, and you define, create, and apply user-defined tags. You must a=
ctivate both types of tags separately before they can appear in Cost Explor=
er or on a cost allocation report.</p>

